From: chumby <chumby@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] tjpgd: enable output scaling

libchumby decodes logos and cover art with jd_decomp() at 1/2..1/8
scale: a 600 px cover for a 92 px tile is a fraction of the work on the
Chumby's ARM9. jd_prepare() now sets the scale to 0, which LVGL's own
decoder (jd_mcu_output() directly, never jd_decomp()) relies on.

--- a/src/libs/tjpgd/tjpgd.c
+++ b/src/libs/tjpgd/tjpgd.c
@@ -960,6 +960,7 @@
     jd->sz_pool = sz_pool;  /* Size of given work memory */
     jd->infunc = infunc;    /* Stream input function */
     jd->device = dev;       /* I/O device identifier */
+    jd->scale = 0;          /* Full size, unless jd_decomp() says (LVGL uses jd_mcu_output() directly) */

     jd->inbuf = seg = alloc_pool(jd, JD_SZBUF);     /* Allocate stream input buffer */
     if(!seg) return JDR_MEM1;
--- a/src/libs/tjpgd/tjpgdcnf.h
+++ b/src/libs/tjpgd/tjpgdcnf.h
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 /  2: Grayscale (8-bit/pix)
 */

-#define JD_USE_SCALE    0
+#define JD_USE_SCALE    1
 /* Switches output descaling feature.
 /  0: Disable
 /  1: Enable
